  },
  "ingredients": [
    "16 ounce brussels sprouts",
    "1/3 medium onion",
    "7 ounce bacon",
    "1 tablespoon olive oil",
    "1/2 cup chicken broth",
    "1 tablespoon butter",
    "2 teaspoon fresh garlic (minced)",
    "salt and pepper (to taste)"
  ],
  "instructions": [
    {
      "text": "Halve your Brussels sprouts by cutting down the white spine. Set these aside for later.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/garlic-and-bacon-brussels-sprouts/#wprm-recipe-50417-step-0-0",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2013/11/garlic-and-bacon-brussels-sprouts-step-01.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Finely dice the the onion. Set these aside with the Brussels sprouts.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/garlic-and-bacon-brussels-sprouts/#wprm-recipe-50417-step-0-1",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2013/11/garlic-and-bacon-brussels-sprouts-step-02.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Take the bacon and cut it into squares. Heat a pan to medium-high and add olive oil. Right as the oil begins to smoke, add the bacon.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/garlic-and-bacon-brussels-sprouts/#wprm-recipe-50417-step-0-2",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2013/11/garlic-and-bacon-brussels-sprouts-step-03.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Let the bacon cook down until the fat has started to render. Remove the bacon and let it rest on a paper towel, trying to keep as much fat in the pan as possible.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/garlic-and-bacon-brussels-sprouts/#wprm-recipe-50417-step-0-3",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2013/11/garlic-and-bacon-brussels-sprouts-step-04.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Add butter to the pan with the bacon grease and let it start to brown.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/garlic-and-bacon-brussels-sprouts/#wprm-recipe-50417-step-0-4",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2013/11/garlic-and-bacon-brussels-sprouts-step-05.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Once the butter begins to brown, add the minced garlic. Wait about 30 seconds, then add the diced onion. Let them cook until they are semi-translucent.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/garlic-and-bacon-brussels-sprouts/#wprm-recipe-50417-step-0-5",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2013/11/garlic-and-bacon-brussels-sprouts-step-06.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Add the Brussels sprouts in and add the salt and pepper. Mix well, so that every single Brussels sprout has a coating of fat. Let this cook for about 4-5 minutes, until they are starting to brown. Add the chicken stock to the pan and mix well. Cover with a lid. Let them absorb all the fats and chicken broth, stirring once 10 minutes in. Check to see if the liquid has been absorbed by creating a hole between the Brussels sprouts.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/garlic-and-bacon-brussels-sprouts/#wprm-recipe-50417-step-0-6",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2013/11/garlic-and-bacon-brussels-sprouts-step-07.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "When Brussels sprouts are ready, add the bacon! Mix well and serve hot.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/garlic-and-bacon-brussels-sprouts/#wprm-recipe-50417-step-0-7",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2013/11/garlic-and-bacon-brussels-sprouts-step-08.jpg"
    }
  ],
